>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_safe_solver`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.add_safe_solver : TraverseExt.ssolver ->
  simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Appends a named safe solver unless a safe solver of that name is installed.
Safe solvers are final solvers of `GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = true}` and are never
used for side conditions. Contexts and solver types belong to `TraverseExt`.

### Failure

Never fails at installation.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>> val decide : TraverseExt.ssolver = {name = "decide", solve = K DECIDE};
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.add_safe_solver decide ext_bool_ss;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = true} ss [] ([], “x < x + 1”) c;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC`](#simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC),
[`simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver),
[`simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers`](#simpExtLib.set_safe_solvers),
[`simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss`](#simpExtLib.safe_solver_ss).
